---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — SFBrews"
  description="About SFBrews, our homebrewing setup, and brewing notes."
>
  <div class="outer page-wrap">
    <div class="canvas prose">
      <h1>About SFBrews</h1>
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>SFBrews</strong>—a personal homebrewing journal documenting recipes, brewday logs, experiments, and competition results.
      </p>

      <h2>The Brewhouse</h2>
      <p>
        <em>Update this section in <code>src/pages/about.astro</code> with your equipment details, batch sizes, and brewing philosophy:</em>
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>System &amp; Batch Size:</strong> KegLand BrewZilla Gen 4.1.1 all-in-one brewing system [add your typical batch volume &amp; accessories]</li>
        <li><strong>Fermentation:</strong> [Add your fermenters and temperature control setup]</li>
        <li><strong>Dispense &amp; Packaging:</strong> [Add your kegging / tap or bottling setup]</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Adding &amp; Updating Posts</h2>
      <p>
        Every writeup lives as a Markdown file in <code>src/content/posts/</code>, with starter templates available in <code>_templates/</code>. Set <code>hidden: true</code> (or a future <code>publishAfter</code> date) in the frontmatter to keep drafts or upcoming competition entries hidden until you are ready to publish.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-wrap {
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }

  .page-wrap h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .page-wrap {
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
